WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(applause)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:05.320
- Let's see what made
Drew's News mood board.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.250
First, in a new piece on Vogue.com,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.250
a young millennial writer
says she got a landline

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.370
and it changed her life.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.490
Yeah!

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.870
The essay covers all the
benefits landlines are great for,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.340
working from home,

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.800
they work in an emergency

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.750
except for mine who's attached to cable

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.873
so when the power goes
out, it all goes out

00:00:27.873 --> 00:00:30.650
and they give your sweet little peepers

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.726
a break from that cell phone

00:00:31.726 --> 00:00:35.130
that you just can't stop staring at.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.250
Okay, now for those young
people watching at home

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.360
who think, what is this?

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.840
This is a telephone

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.650
and I'm here to show you how it's done.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.213
First, you pick up the receiver,

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.060
(sighs)

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:50.893
that's right,

00:00:50.893 --> 00:00:52.200
that's this part right here.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.790
And then you think of
your bestie's phone number

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:57.673
which you have saved in your mind.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.967
It's seven digits if
they're local (clicking),

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.403
11 if they're in a
different area code, 310.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:10.230
Now in the 917-212's, oh yeah, 212,

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.180
that's a hot area code.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.719
While the other side rings,

00:01:13.719 --> 00:01:17.630
you can fiddle with this
curly thing we call a cord

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.970
and then your bestie picks up

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:22.920
and you talk about boys and girls and life

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.400
and it's like the best.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.290
It's a thing of beauty

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.350
and I'm so glad that
they're making a comeback,

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.443
by the way, this is my
personal phone from my bedroom.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:37.184
There are two stories
that I love to follow,

00:01:37.184 --> 00:01:38.920
two sites, excuse me,

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.240
one is Tank's Good News

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.430
and he'll be here on the
show with us this month

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.090
and another is Upworthy,

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.230
and if you're not following
either of these sites,

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.286
trust me, I really believe

00:01:47.286 --> 00:01:50.350
that they will make
your life happier, okay.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.870
So go to our website and I'll
link you to both of them.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.660
So I saw this post on Upworthy

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.210
and it gave a woman,
oh, that's what it is,

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:02.400
a woman she gave serious
thought to her LinkedIn profile.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.860
Lauren G saw her perfectly
polished power pose

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.350
and it didn't,

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.810
and she didn't feel like it
portrayed who she really was,

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.560
and so, to show some authenticity,

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.200
she replaced it with a
less professional one

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.290
and put up a much more real pic

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.610
of a mom balancing everything in her life.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.647
Lauren, I think you really represent

00:02:21.647 --> 00:02:24.810
how a lot of people feel this year.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.930
Okay, let's lift up the veil,

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.236
get rid of the veneer

00:02:28.236 --> 00:02:31.296
and proudly be our authentic self.

00:02:31.296 --> 00:02:32.129
(applause)

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:33.580
Thank you, Lauren G.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.420
I know, I love this.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:39.934
Oh! Time for a beauty junkie alert.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.980
(applause)

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.700
So guess what? It's official,

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.220
banana clips are back, okay.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.053
Yeah.

00:02:48.053 --> 00:02:50.070
The New York Post reports
that the banana clip

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.630
has seen increased interest

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.670
and getting Googled and
pinned more than ever.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.371
How scary that they know that?

00:02:55.371 --> 00:02:56.204
(audience laughs)

00:02:56.204 --> 00:02:57.570
It might not seem wow worthy,

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.960
but just check out this hairstyle

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.560
Kristen Bell rocked with this bad boy.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.540
Yeah, I think that's super foxy.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.420
Banana clips are wow worthy.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.853
Oh, and speaking of bananas,

00:03:08.853 --> 00:03:11.290
we had to say goodbye to Carole Baskin,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.580
the cat queen herself on
Dancing With The Stars.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.130
She gave it her all though

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.170
and for her last dance,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.107
she performed the samba
to the "Circle of Life"

00:03:19.107 --> 00:03:22.783
dressed as a lion because of course,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.820
Carole Baskin, lion,

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:29.000
so, so long for now,
you cool cat and kitten.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:29.960
Oh my God, by the way,

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.874
if you need more Tiger
King 'cause everybody does,

00:03:32.874 --> 00:03:34.900
check out the documentary special

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.300
